#X text 430 346 layer 1: each neuron mixes X and Y and bends the result, f 60;
#X text 430 466 layer 2: mixes of mixes, f 60;
#X text 430 586 outputs: pitch \, FM ratio \, FM depth \, brightness, f 60;
#X obj 10 756 cnv 1 1260 250 empty empty THE\ INSTRUMENT:\ the\ 4\ outputs\ play\ a\ 2-operator\ FM\ voice 8 12 0 13 #fff1e0 #1d3557 0;
#N canvas 40 60 1100 560 fm-voice 0;
#X text 20 10 FM synthesis (Chowning 1973): a modulator oscillator wobbles the frequency of a carrier. The network outputs (-1..+1) are scaled into: 1) pitch \, MIDI 36..72 2) ratio modulator/carrier 1..5 (non-integers = bell-like) 3) FM index 0..8 (how much wobble = how bright) 4) lowpass cutoff 200..5000 Hz., f 140;
#X obj 20 70 inlet~;
#X obj 240 70 inlet~;
#X obj 460 70 inlet~;
#X obj 680 70 inlet~;
#X text 80 70 pitch, f 10;
#X text 300 70 ratio, f 10;
#X text 520 70 index, f 10;
#X text 740 70 cutoff, f 10;
#X obj 20 100 expr~ 54 + 18 * \$v1;
#X obj 20 126 mtof~;
#X obj 240 100 expr~ 3 + 2 * \$v1;
#X obj 460 100 expr~ 4 + 4 * \$v1;
#X obj 680 100 expr~ 2600 + 2400 * \$v1;
#X obj 240 160 *~;
#X obj 240 190 osc~;
#X obj 460 190 *~;
#X obj 240 220 *~;
